UPDATE questions SET explanation = '<div class=\"explanation-rich-content\"><div class=\"expl-card concept-card\"><div class=\"section-title-concept\">📌 Core Concept: Assured Forwarding Values - AF43</div><p>Assured Forwarding classes use the formula DSCP (Differentiated Services Code Point) = 8 x class + 2 x drop precedence. AFxy means class x, drop precedence y. A higher drop precedence means the packet is more likely to be dropped when the queue is congested.</p></div><div class=\"expl-card correct-card\"><h4 class=\"section-title-correct\">✓ Why the Correct Answer (Option B) is Correct:</h4><ul><li><span class=\"opt-tag correct\">Option B</span> <strong>38</strong>: AF43 is DSCP 38.</li></ul></div><div class=\"expl-card incorrect-card\"><h4 class=\"section-title-incorrect\">✗ Why Other Options are Incorrect:</h4><ul><li><span class=\"opt-tag wrong\">Option A</span> <strong>40</strong>: DSCP 40 is the value for CS5, not for AF43.</li><li><span class=\"opt-tag wrong\">Option C</span> <strong>36</strong>: DSCP 36 is the value for AF42, not for AF43.</li><li><span class=\"opt-tag wrong\">Option D</span> <strong>34</strong>: DSCP 34 is the value for AF41, not for AF43.</li></ul></div><div class=\"expl-card tip-card\"><h4 class=\"section-title-tip\">💡 CCNA Exam Tip:</h4><p>Memorise the formula:</p><ul><li>CSx = 8x.</li><li>AFxy = 8x + 2y.</li><li>EF = 46.</li><li>DF = 0.</li></ul></div><div class=\"expl-card concept-card\"><div class=\"section-title-concept\">📋 IPv4 Header - Full Reference (Memorize This):</div><table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin-top:8px;font-size:13px;\"><tr><td colspan=\"4\" style=\"border:1px solid #4a5568;padding:6px;text-align:center;\">Version<br><span style=\"font-size:12px;\">4 bits</span></td><td colspan=\"4\" style=\"border:1px solid #4a5568;padding:6px;text-align:center;\">IHL<br><span style=\"font-size:12px;\">4 bits</span></td><td colspan=\"6\" style=\"border:1px solid #4a5568;padding:6px;text-align:center;\">DSCP<br><span style=\"font-size:12px;\">6 bits</span></td><td colspan=\"2\" style=\"border:1px solid #4a5568;padding:6px;text-align:center;\">ECN<br><span style=\"font-size:12px;\">2 bits</span></td><td colspan=\"16\" style=\"border:1px solid #4a5568;padding:6px;text-align:center;\">Total Length<br><span style=\"font-size:12px;\">16 bits</span></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"16\" style=\"border:1px solid #4a5568;padding:6px;text-align:center;\">Identification<br><span style=\"font-size:12px;\">16 bits</span></td><td colspan=\"3\" style=\"border:1px solid #4a5568;padding:6px;text-align:center;\">Flags<br><span style=\"font-size:12px;\">3 bits</span></td><td colspan=\"13\" style=\"border:1px solid #4a5568;padding:6px;text-align:center;\">Fragment Offset<br><span style=\"font-size:12px;\">13 bits</span></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"8\" style=\"border:1px solid #4a5568;padding:6px;text-align:center;\">TTL<br><span style=\"font-size:12px;\">8 bits</span></td><td colspan=\"8\" style=\"border:1px solid #4a5568;padding:6px;text-align:center;\">Protocol<br><span style=\"font-size:12px;\">8 bits</span></td><td colspan=\"16\" style=\"border:1px solid #4a5568;padding:6px;text-align:center;\">Header Checksum<br><span style=\"font-size:12px;\">16 bits</span></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"32\" style=\"border:1px solid #4a5568;padding:6px;text-align:center;\">Source Address<br><span style=\"font-size:12px;\">32 bits</span></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"32\" style=\"border:1px solid #4a5568;padding:6px;text-align:center;\">Destination Address<br><span style=\"font-size:12px;\">32 bits</span></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"32\" style=\"border:1px solid #4a5568;padding:6px;text-align:center;\">Options + Padding<br><span style=\"font-size:12px;\">0-40 bytes</span></td></tr></table><div style=\"font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;margin-top:10px;\"><div style=\"margin-bottom:7px;\"><strong>Version</strong> <span style=\"opacity:0.75;\">(4 bits)</span>: IP version (4)</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:7px;\"><strong>IHL (Internet Header Length)</strong> <span style=\"opacity:0.75;\">(4 bits)</span>: Header length in 32-bit words (5-15); IHL × 4 = header bytes (20-60)</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:7px;\"><strong>DSCP (Differentiated Services Code Point)</strong> <span style=\"opacity:0.75;\">(6 bits)</span>: QoS marking (0-63)</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:7px;\"><strong>ECN (Explicit Congestion Notification)</strong> <span style=\"opacity:0.75;\">(2 bits)</span>: Congestion notification (0-3)</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:7px;\"><strong>Total Length</strong> <span style=\"opacity:0.75;\">(16 bits)</span>: Whole packet length in bytes, header + data (max 65,535)</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:7px;\"><strong>Identification</strong> <span style=\"opacity:0.75;\">(16 bits)</span>: Same ID for all fragments of one packet</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:7px;\"><strong>Flags</strong> <span style=\"opacity:0.75;\">(3 bits)</span>: Reserved (0), DF (Don\'t Fragment), MF (More Fragments)</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:7px;\"><strong>Fragment Offset</strong> <span style=\"opacity:0.75;\">(13 bits)</span>: Position of this fragment in the original packet (in 8-byte units)</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:7px;\"><strong>TTL (Time to Live)</strong> <span style=\"opacity:0.75;\">(8 bits)</span>: Max hops; each router subtracts 1, drops the packet at 0</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:7px;\"><strong>Protocol</strong> <span style=\"opacity:0.75;\">(8 bits)</span>: Next protocol: 1 = ICMP (Internet Control Message Protocol), 6 = TCP (Transmission Control Protocol), 17 = UDP (User Datagram Protocol), 89 = OSPF (Open Shortest Path First)</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:7px;\"><strong>Header Checksum</strong> <span style=\"opacity:0.75;\">(16 bits)</span>: Error check on the header only (recalculated at each hop)</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:7px;\"><strong>Source Address</strong> <span style=\"opacity:0.75;\">(32 bits)</span>: Sender IPv4 (Internet Protocol version 4) address</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:7px;\"><strong>Destination Address</strong> <span style=\"opacity:0.75;\">(32 bits)</span>: Receiver IPv4 address</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:7px;\"><strong>Options</strong> <span style=\"opacity:0.75;\">(0-40 bytes)</span>: Rarely used (e.g. Record Route, Timestamp); Padding pads the header to a multiple of 32 bits</div></div><p style=\"margin-top:8px;\">Total: 20 bytes minimum, up to 60 bytes with Options. IHL × 4 = header length in bytes.</p></div><div class=\"expl-card concept-card\"><div class=\"section-title-concept\">📌 Source: Anki Flashcards - IP Services (CCNA / Day 47 Flashcards - QoS (Part 2)</div></div></div>' WHERE question_no = 'Anki-IPS-4369';

