UPDATE questions SET explanation = '<div class=\"explanation-rich-content\"><div class=\"expl-card concept-card\"><div class=\"section-title-concept\">📌 Core Concept: Assured Forwarding Values - AF31</div><p>Assured Forwarding classes use the formula DSCP (Differentiated Services Code Point) = 8 x class + 2 x drop precedence. AFxy means class x, drop precedence y. A higher drop precedence means the packet is more likely to be dropped when the queue is congested.</p></div><div class=\"expl-card correct-card\"><h4 class=\"section-title-correct\">✓ Why the Correct Answer (Option B) is Correct:</h4><ul><li><span class=\"opt-tag correct\">Option B</span> <strong>26</strong>: AF31 is DSCP 26.</li></ul></div><div class=\"expl-card incorrect-card\"><h4 class=\"section-title-incorrect\">✗ Why Other Options are Incorrect:</h4><ul><li><span class=\"opt-tag wrong\">Option A</span> <strong>28</strong>: DSCP 28 is the value for AF32, not for AF31.</li><li><span class=\"opt-tag wrong\">Option C</span> <strong>30</strong>: DSCP 30 is the value for AF33, not for AF31.</li><li><span class=\"opt-tag wrong\">Option D</span> <strong>24</strong>: DSCP 24 is the value for CS3, not for AF31.</li></ul></div><div class=\"expl-card tip-card\"><h4 class=\"section-title-tip\">💡 CCNA Exam Tip:</h4><p>Memorise the formula:</p><ul><li>CSx = 8x.</li><li>AFxy = 8x + 2y.</li><li>EF = 46.</li><li>DF = 0.</li></ul></div><div class=\"expl-card concept-card\"><div class=\"section-title-concept\">📋 IPv4 Header - Full Reference (Memorize This):</div><table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin-top:8px;font-size:13px;\"><tr><td colspan=\"4\" style=\"border:1px solid #4a5568;padding:6px;text-align:center;\">Version<br><span style=\"font-size:12px;\">4 bits</span></td><td colspan=\"4\" style=\"border:1px solid #4a5568;padding:6px;text-align:center;\">IHL<br><span style=\"font-size:12px;\">4 bits</span></td><td colspan=\"6\" style=\"border:1px solid #4a5568;padding:6px;text-align:center;\">DSCP<br