L (Internet Header Length)</strong> <span style=\"opacity:0.75;\">(4 bits)</span>: Header length in 32-bit words (5-15); IHL × 4 = header bytes (20-60)</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:7px;\"><strong>DSCP (Differentiated Services Code Point)</strong> <span style=\"opacity:0.75;\">(6 bits)</span>: QoS marking (0-63)</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:7px;\"><strong>ECN (Explicit Congestion Notification)</strong> <span style=\"opacity:0.75;\">(2 bits)</span>: Congestion notification (0-3)</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:7px;\"><strong>Total Length</strong> <span style=\"opacity:0.75;\">(16 bits)</span>: Whole packet length in bytes, header + data (max 65,535)</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:7px;\"><strong>Identification</strong> <span style=\"opacity:0.75;\">(16 bits)</span>: Same ID for all fragments of one packet</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:7px;\"><strong>Flags</strong> <span style=\"opacity:0.75;\">(3 bits)</span>: Reserved (0), DF (Don\'t Fragment), MF (More Fragments)</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:7px;\"><strong>Fragment Offset</strong> <span style=\"opacity:0.75;\">(13 bits)</span>: Position of this fragment in the original packet (in 8-byte units)</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:7px;\"><strong>TTL (Time to Live)</strong> <span style=\"opacity:0.75;\">(8 bits)</span>: Max hops; each router subtracts 1, drops the packet at 0</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:7px;\"><strong>Protocol</strong> <span style=\"opacity:0.75;\">(8 bits)</span>: Next protocol: 1 = ICMP (Internet Control Message Protocol), 6 = TCP (Transmission Control Protocol), 17 = UDP (User Datagram Protocol), 89 = OSPF (Open Shortest Path First)</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:7px;\"><strong>Header Checksum</strong> <span style=\"opacity:0.75;\">(16 bits)</span>: Error check on the header only (recalculated at each hop)</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:7px;\"><strong>Source Address</strong> <span style=\"opacity:0.75;\">(32 bits)</span>: Sender IPv4 (Internet Protocol version 4) address</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:7px;\"><strong>Destination Address</strong> <span style=\"opacity:0.75;\">(32 bits)</span>: Receiver IPv4 address</div><div style=\"margin-bottom:7px;\"><strong>Options</strong> <span style=\"opacity:0.75;\">(0-40 bytes)</span>: Rarely used (e.g. Record Route, Timestamp); Padding pads the header to a multiple of 32 bits</div></div><p style=\"margin-top:8px;\">Total: 20 bytes minimum, up to 60 bytes with Options. IHL × 4 = header length in bytes.</p></div><div class=\"expl-card concept-card\"><div class=\"section-title-concept\">📌 Source: Anki Flashcards - IP Services (CCNA / Day 47 Flashcards - QoS (Part 2)</div></div></div>' WHERE question_no = 'Anki-IPS-4376';

